WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:03.320
- She started out studying
aeronautical engineering,

00:00:03.320 --> 00:00:04.170
which I did not know,

00:00:04.170 --> 00:00:07.620
and went on to become Miss World, okay.

00:00:07.620 --> 00:00:09.730
One of "Times" most influential people,

00:00:09.730 --> 00:00:12.740
one of "Forbes" most
powerful women, and a Jonas.

00:00:12.740 --> 00:00:14.270
I'm just saying that's a lot of checks.

00:00:14.270 --> 00:00:16.130
It's a lot of boxes she's checked.

00:00:16.130 --> 00:00:19.390
Her new memoir is called
"Unfinished" great title.

00:00:19.390 --> 00:00:22.742
Let's say hello to Miss
Priyanka Chopra Jonas!

00:00:22.742 --> 00:00:25.409
(upbeat music)

00:00:27.080 --> 00:00:28.390
Hello!

00:00:28.390 --> 00:00:30.430
- Hi Kelly, how are you?

00:00:30.430 --> 00:00:31.370
- I'm so good.

00:00:31.370 --> 00:00:34.290
Your husband was talking
smack on our group texts

00:00:34.290 --> 00:00:36.510
the other day, our "Voice" group text.

00:00:36.510 --> 00:00:38.187
He was like, "You losers ready?

00:00:38.187 --> 00:00:39.906
"I'm gonna come and beat"

00:00:39.906 --> 00:00:40.930
I was like, all right, Jonas.

00:00:40.930 --> 00:00:43.010
But I've seen you a
couple of times on set.

00:00:43.010 --> 00:00:44.080
We never get to talk too long.

00:00:44.080 --> 00:00:46.300
'Cause we're always running
for the camera or whatever.

00:00:46.300 --> 00:00:47.780
But do you like coming?

00:00:47.780 --> 00:00:48.800
Do you enjoy it?

00:00:48.800 --> 00:00:51.620
I loved how our compound used
to be and we could all hang.

00:00:51.620 --> 00:00:53.200
That's no longer.

00:00:53.200 --> 00:00:54.760
- I just miss human interaction.

00:00:54.760 --> 00:00:56.920
I swear the first time I
thought I'd be seeing you

00:00:56.920 --> 00:00:58.470
on your show would be on that couch.

00:00:58.470 --> 00:01:00.140
And like, we'd be sitting
together, you know,

00:01:00.140 --> 00:01:02.040
having a drink, talking,

00:01:02.040 --> 00:01:03.790
like we usually do whenever we meet.

00:01:03.790 --> 00:01:06.000
And you know, it's a weird world.

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:07.770
And I love coming to
the set of "The Voice".

00:01:07.770 --> 00:01:09.140
I was actually a fan of the show

00:01:09.140 --> 00:01:11.300
before Nick even came onto the show.

00:01:11.300 --> 00:01:12.810
I'd watched it so many times.

00:01:12.810 --> 00:01:14.720
I told him when he needs to like,

00:01:14.720 --> 00:01:16.450
how much time he needs to sort of take

00:01:16.450 --> 00:01:18.750
before he turns the chair
and stuff like that.

00:01:19.840 --> 00:01:21.010
- I love it, I love it.

00:01:21.010 --> 00:01:22.990
Well, do you remember this moment?

00:01:22.990 --> 00:01:24.560
Because I do.

00:01:24.560 --> 00:01:26.450
You helped me out.

00:01:26.450 --> 00:01:28.133
So do you remember that?

00:01:29.920 --> 00:01:31.050
- I do remember that.

00:01:31.050 --> 00:01:32.750
You were gonna go back on stage

00:01:32.750 --> 00:01:35.740
and this was the variety of women-

00:01:35.740 --> 00:01:36.915
- Power of Women, yeah.

00:01:36.915 --> 00:01:37.817
- Power lunch or something, wasn't it.

00:01:37.817 --> 00:01:38.820
- Yeah.
- Power of Women.

00:01:38.820 --> 00:01:42.570
- And that was the first time
we met, and you were so nice.

00:01:42.570 --> 00:01:44.520
Literally, I was like, she was so nice,

00:01:44.520 --> 00:01:45.770
she's such a girl's girl.

00:01:45.770 --> 00:01:47.650
I was sweating, I had just
gotten off stage performing.

00:01:47.650 --> 00:01:49.090
I was about to go do another thing.

00:01:49.090 --> 00:01:50.821
And I was like, oh my God, I'm so sweaty.

00:01:50.821 --> 00:01:52.277
And I had nothing, and
you totally touched me up.

00:01:52.277 --> 00:01:53.510
Has there been another time-

00:01:53.510 --> 00:01:55.380
- But it's also the Indian in me, I think.

00:01:55.380 --> 00:01:56.460
It's a very cultural thing to me

00:01:56.460 --> 00:01:58.700
to be all up in your
business, and be like,

00:01:58.700 --> 00:01:59.950
let me just get you, come here, come here,

00:01:59.950 --> 00:02:03.481
show me your face, clean you
up, all right, go on ahead.

00:02:03.481 --> 00:02:04.314
It's very cultural.

00:02:04.314 --> 00:02:07.120
- Well, it's very Southern
as well, like where I'm from.

00:02:07.120 --> 00:02:09.220
So I thought it was really, really nice.

00:02:09.220 --> 00:02:10.100
Is there another time-

00:02:10.100 --> 00:02:11.610
- I'm glad you did.

00:02:11.610 --> 00:02:13.220
- Oh, I loved it.

00:02:13.220 --> 00:02:15.220
Well, I'm a major extrovert,
if you haven't noticed.

00:02:15.220 --> 00:02:17.194
So I love extroverts.

00:02:17.194 --> 00:02:19.410
And you and Nick had your
second anniversary recently.

00:02:19.410 --> 00:02:20.808
That's amazing.

00:02:20.808 --> 00:02:22.850
I feel like sometimes
when couples are together,

00:02:22.850 --> 00:02:26.450
you start to like be like each
other, are y'all that yet?

00:02:26.450 --> 00:02:29.390
- Well, I have become a lot
neater than I used to be.

00:02:29.390 --> 00:02:31.120
I put my shoes together now,

00:02:31.120 --> 00:02:32.550
'cause he puts his shoes together.

00:02:32.550 --> 00:02:34.650
And I don't wanna be the one who's a mess.

00:02:35.690 --> 00:02:39.150
I eat on the dining table
now, which I hated doing.

00:02:39.150 --> 00:02:43.260
I used to love eating on the
couch in my blanket, you know?

00:02:43.260 --> 00:02:45.460
But he likes to sit on the dining table.

00:02:45.460 --> 00:02:47.910
So I've started becoming
a little bit like that.

00:02:47.910 --> 00:02:50.050
Yeah, so I think I'm
the one who's changed.

00:02:50.050 --> 00:02:51.730
- No, I love that though.

00:02:51.730 --> 00:02:53.890
Totally, his personality,
I would have totally

00:02:53.890 --> 00:02:57.880
expected him to be like
a clean freak, yeah.

00:02:57.880 --> 00:03:00.210
- Even his closet, like all the hangers

00:03:00.210 --> 00:03:01.680
are sort of distanced together.

00:03:01.680 --> 00:03:04.780
And mine's like a drawer
full of just clothes.

00:03:04.780 --> 00:03:06.370
- Oh my God, I love that, I love that.

00:03:06.370 --> 00:03:08.390
All right, we're back.

00:03:08.390 --> 00:03:09.950
And I was watching, I almost made us stop

00:03:09.950 --> 00:03:11.520
because you had like a sneezing attack

00:03:11.520 --> 00:03:12.920
or something I could see.

00:03:12.920 --> 00:03:14.190
But I almost held off-

00:03:14.190 --> 00:03:15.920
- No, I had a-

00:03:15.920 --> 00:03:17.490
I was drinking, I'm not crying.

00:03:17.490 --> 00:03:21.290
I was drinking some water and
it went down the wrong side.

00:03:21.290 --> 00:03:22.910
- Oh my God, I was
like, somebody help her,

00:03:22.910 --> 00:03:24.290
but you couldn't hear me.

00:03:24.290 --> 00:03:26.800
And I was like, I hate this virtual world.

00:03:26.800 --> 00:03:29.190
I was like, she's choking!

00:03:29.190 --> 00:03:31.770
Anyway, we've got Priyanka
Chopra Jonas on Skype, y'all,

00:03:31.770 --> 00:03:33.020
and she's alive and well.

00:03:34.690 --> 00:03:37.007
- I'm okay, I'm okay.

00:03:37.007 --> 00:03:39.740
- I'm okay, well
congratulations on the book.

00:03:39.740 --> 00:03:41.327
This is amazing.

00:03:41.327 --> 00:03:43.400
I mean, coming from a writer

00:03:43.400 --> 00:03:45.140
that writes about her own life sometimes,

00:03:45.140 --> 00:03:47.290
that is a very hard thing to do sometimes

00:03:47.290 --> 00:03:48.580
with certain subject matters.

00:03:48.580 --> 00:03:52.100
So was it hard for you to
write about your own life?

00:03:52.100 --> 00:03:53.030
- It definitely was.

00:03:53.030 --> 00:03:54.820
I actually always wanted to write a book.

00:03:54.820 --> 00:03:56.430
And I thought that the easiest thing

00:03:56.430 --> 00:03:58.137
would be to write a memoir,

00:03:58.137 --> 00:03:58.970
because you know your life, you know?

00:03:58.970 --> 00:04:02.310
But it's not because
you end up dealing with

00:04:02.310 --> 00:04:03.623
and talking about things

00:04:05.795 --> 00:04:06.628
that you kind of buried in your past

00:04:06.628 --> 00:04:08.478
and haven't thought about for a long time.

00:04:08.478 --> 00:04:11.760
And I wrote it at a time
which was daunting as well.

00:04:11.760 --> 00:04:13.890
I wrote it in 2020 during quarantine,

00:04:13.890 --> 00:04:16.620
because I had the luxury
of the time to write it.

00:04:16.620 --> 00:04:18.510
So I was emotional, vulnerable

00:04:18.510 --> 00:04:20.250
and kind of reflected in the book.

00:04:20.250 --> 00:04:23.992
It's so much more personal
than I ever intended it to be.

00:04:23.992 --> 00:04:26.150
- Yeah, 'cause writing for me,

00:04:26.150 --> 00:04:27.530
especially when I'm
writing songs about my own,

00:04:27.530 --> 00:04:30.470
it's kind of therapeutic for
me, and it can be overwhelming.

00:04:30.470 --> 00:04:31.303
- Totally.

00:04:31.303 --> 00:04:32.540
- But was it therapeutic for you?

00:04:32.540 --> 00:04:34.472
Did you kind of like go man,
I forgot that even happened.

00:04:34.472 --> 00:04:36.810
- I think it was healing.
- Oh, that's so good.

00:04:36.810 --> 00:04:37.643
- Very much.

00:04:37.643 --> 00:04:41.333
So I feel like I've been
running so fast in my life.

00:04:42.240 --> 00:04:44.860
2020 was 20 years in the
entertainment business for me.

00:04:44.860 --> 00:04:47.730
So I realized that I'd only

00:04:47.730 --> 00:04:50.260
been running from one job to the next.

00:04:50.260 --> 00:04:54.657
As you know, in our jobs
you don't know what the...

00:04:54.657 --> 00:04:57.909
It's not consistent like a normal job.

00:04:57.909 --> 00:04:59.320
You have to figure out
what the next job is,

00:04:59.320 --> 00:05:00.810
to where your check's coming from.

00:05:00.810 --> 00:05:03.425
Like there's a constant hustle.

00:05:03.425 --> 00:05:04.440
And I'd been running to make sure

00:05:04.440 --> 00:05:06.640
that I had a consistent
career for such a long time.

00:05:06.640 --> 00:05:09.680
I didn't think about a lot of
things, or deal with things

00:05:09.680 --> 00:05:13.650
that may have been hard,
or rejections or failures.

00:05:13.650 --> 00:05:16.610
And writing a book
really helps you do that.

00:05:16.610 --> 00:05:18.460
So it was super healing for me.

00:05:18.460 --> 00:05:19.410
- That's incredible.

00:05:19.410 --> 00:05:22.530
What a blessing.
- It really was.

00:05:22.530 --> 00:05:26.340
- Yeah, you write a lot about
your childhood in India.

00:05:26.340 --> 00:05:27.940
So what's going on with this picture?

00:05:27.940 --> 00:05:29.063
I love this photo.

00:05:31.040 --> 00:05:31.873
What is that?

00:05:31.873 --> 00:05:33.840
What's happening?

00:05:33.840 --> 00:05:35.680
- I was a year, I think,
a year and a half.

00:05:35.680 --> 00:05:38.520
But this is me wearing my
dad's military uniform.

00:05:38.520 --> 00:05:40.460
I was obsessed with my father.

00:05:40.460 --> 00:05:41.660
I wanted to be him.

00:05:41.660 --> 00:05:43.570
He had long legs, he was tall,

00:05:43.570 --> 00:05:45.820
he was funny, he was charming.

00:05:45.820 --> 00:05:47.270
And this was his uniform.

00:05:47.270 --> 00:05:49.790
And I just always used to dress myself.

00:05:49.790 --> 00:05:52.132
I used to wear his shoes,
I used to where his beret.

00:05:52.132 --> 00:05:55.480
That's how I felt closest to him.

00:05:55.480 --> 00:05:56.313
- That's amazing.

00:05:56.313 --> 00:05:58.520
That's an awesome relationship.

00:05:58.520 --> 00:06:00.230
Well, tell me about the plan

00:06:00.230 --> 00:06:02.103
your brother had to get
you out of the house.

00:06:02.103 --> 00:06:04.590
That was my favorite part,
like reading about this was,

00:06:04.590 --> 00:06:06.210
his trick to get you out of the house

00:06:06.210 --> 00:06:08.223
kind of catapulted your career, right?

00:06:09.330 --> 00:06:11.823
- It kind of really set me on this track.

00:06:13.450 --> 00:06:15.600
I had just moved back to
India from the States.

00:06:15.600 --> 00:06:18.500
And there were only two other
rooms in my parents' house.

00:06:18.500 --> 00:06:22.640
And you know, my brother's
room was kind of given to me,

00:06:22.640 --> 00:06:25.244
because I was a 16 year
old teenager at that point.

00:06:25.244 --> 00:06:27.460
And obviously, I didn't argue with that.

00:06:27.460 --> 00:06:30.250
But he wanted his room back
because my mom had set him up

00:06:30.250 --> 00:06:33.090
in the hallway between the two rooms.

00:06:33.090 --> 00:06:35.817
And I had just gotten some photos taken,

00:06:35.817 --> 00:06:37.610
like, you know mall shots,

00:06:37.610 --> 00:06:41.560
the soft focus, like hand on
your face kind of pictures?

00:06:41.560 --> 00:06:44.650
And he took those pictures
at all 10 years old,

00:06:44.650 --> 00:06:46.390
and told my mom, took the magazine

00:06:46.390 --> 00:06:48.240
in which there was a commercial

00:06:48.240 --> 00:06:50.767
for the Miss India pageant. And
he was like, "You know what?

00:06:50.767 --> 00:06:52.317
"Why don't you send her in for this?

00:06:52.317 --> 00:06:54.750
"'Cause then she'll have
to go away to Mumbai."

00:06:54.750 --> 00:06:56.580
In his ten-year-old mind was,

00:06:56.580 --> 00:06:59.790
that was his way of getting his room back.

00:06:59.790 --> 00:07:01.890
And I went into the pageant, won it,

00:07:01.890 --> 00:07:04.610
and that like triggered my entire career,

00:07:04.610 --> 00:07:05.823
as I know it right now.

00:07:06.690 --> 00:07:09.619
- Was that even a dream
of yours, to do a pageant?

00:07:09.619 --> 00:07:14.190
- No, I never even knew
that normal girls could be

00:07:14.190 --> 00:07:18.760
in a pageant, and that's
how it all happened.

00:07:18.760 --> 00:07:20.773
Crazy, yeah.
- That's amazing.

00:07:21.850 --> 00:07:24.770
So I read you were kicked
out of a couple of museums

00:07:24.770 --> 00:07:27.790
which like, I liked you before, Priyanka,

00:07:27.790 --> 00:07:31.770
but I really loved reading
about you before this interview.

00:07:31.770 --> 00:07:34.480
'Cause how were you kicked out of museums?

00:07:34.480 --> 00:07:37.240
- 'Cause you try and
touch the "Starry Night".

00:07:37.240 --> 00:07:40.360
I mean, you can't try
and touch "Starry Night"

00:07:40.360 --> 00:07:42.718
that's like preserved art and-
- You put your hands on it?

00:07:42.718 --> 00:07:45.330
- Yes.
- Oh no.

00:07:45.330 --> 00:07:48.640
- I was kicked out because I touched it.

00:07:48.640 --> 00:07:52.800
And alarms and people, and
my family was embarrassed.

00:07:52.800 --> 00:07:54.700
Even at the Louvre, I
tried to take a picture

00:07:54.700 --> 00:07:55.533
with the "Mona Lisa"

00:07:55.533 --> 00:07:57.500
which wasn't allowed and I got kicked out.

00:07:57.500 --> 00:08:00.850
It was like, what was
wrong with me and art?

00:08:00.850 --> 00:08:05.500
- Those are like really huge
museums, like prestigious.

00:08:05.500 --> 00:08:07.260
- Yeah, not even like the little ones.

00:08:07.260 --> 00:08:09.580
- Yeah, no, hey, that's
kind of cooler though.

00:08:09.580 --> 00:08:12.160
You're kicked out of The
Louvre, like that's kinda cool.

00:08:12.160 --> 00:08:14.080
I wanna ask you about
something that you said

00:08:14.080 --> 00:08:15.630
at the Miss World Competition.

00:08:15.630 --> 00:08:18.550
'Cause I loved it, I fell in love with it.

00:08:18.550 --> 00:08:19.790
The contestants were asked

00:08:19.790 --> 00:08:22.350
to come up with questions
for others to answer,

00:08:22.350 --> 00:08:23.890
which is a lot of pressure, I feel like.

00:08:23.890 --> 00:08:25.380
I kept thinking before I read yours,

00:08:25.380 --> 00:08:26.213
what would I have said?

00:08:26.213 --> 00:08:27.682
Like, what would I have asked?

00:08:27.682 --> 00:08:29.527
And this was so beautifully asked,

00:08:29.527 --> 00:08:33.397
"If ignorance is bliss,
why do we seek knowledge?"

00:08:34.248 --> 00:08:37.163
Like, my joke in life is always like,

00:08:38.010 --> 00:08:39.700
which pill was it in the matrix?

00:08:39.700 --> 00:08:41.570
It was like, I should
have taken the other pill.

00:08:41.570 --> 00:08:43.333
I should have taken the red pill.

00:08:43.333 --> 00:08:44.180
You know what I'm saying?

00:08:44.180 --> 00:08:45.980
Or the blue one, whichever
one was ignorance.

00:08:45.980 --> 00:08:47.610
I was like, maybe that
would have been better.

00:08:47.610 --> 00:08:49.610
And that's always my
private joke to myself.

00:08:49.610 --> 00:08:51.930
And I love that. So what
does that mean to you?

00:08:51.930 --> 00:08:54.020
And why did you ask that?

00:08:54.020 --> 00:08:55.870
- Well, it was such a mean thing to do,

00:08:55.870 --> 00:08:57.070
now that I think about it.

00:08:57.070 --> 00:08:58.430
I was like, why did I have to write

00:08:58.430 --> 00:09:01.790
such a tough question for
someone else to answer?

00:09:01.790 --> 00:09:03.800
But it actually was my question

00:09:03.800 --> 00:09:05.470
during the Miss India Pageant.

00:09:05.470 --> 00:09:08.341
And I remember saying something like,

00:09:08.341 --> 00:09:10.700
if ignorance was bliss, I wouldn't know

00:09:10.700 --> 00:09:14.000
what loving, caring, and
sharing is or some such.

00:09:14.000 --> 00:09:15.210
But when I wrote that down,

00:09:15.210 --> 00:09:17.220
I was like, my mind had gotten blank.

00:09:17.220 --> 00:09:18.910
It was a Miss World contest.

00:09:18.910 --> 00:09:20.960
And I was just like terrified.

00:09:20.960 --> 00:09:22.940
And I just wrote whatever I remembered.

00:09:22.940 --> 00:09:24.240
But she did a great job with it.

00:09:24.240 --> 00:09:27.980
But now in retrospect, it was
just such a mean thing to do.

00:09:27.980 --> 00:09:30.280
- Yeah, I was like you
are seriously competitive,

00:09:30.280 --> 00:09:31.590
asking someone that question.

00:09:31.590 --> 00:09:33.349
You're like, I'm gonna trip her up.

00:09:33.349 --> 00:09:34.182
I'm gonna trip her up.

00:09:34.182 --> 00:09:35.272
I'm taking that crown.
- So mean!

00:09:35.272 --> 00:09:36.870
I'm so mean.

00:09:36.870 --> 00:09:38.380
- No, it's an amazing question.

00:09:38.380 --> 00:09:39.230
It's an important one too,

00:09:39.230 --> 00:09:42.270
'cause it is like such a
thought provoking question,

00:09:42.270 --> 00:09:43.280
to where I think it's one of those

00:09:43.280 --> 00:09:46.150
great conversations starters,
like a dinner or something.

00:09:46.150 --> 00:09:49.460
But everybody, Priyanka's new
book is called "Unfinished"

00:09:49.460 --> 00:09:51.510
and it's out now, you gotta check it out.

